---
import Section from './Section.astro';

// The device run as a reader meets it: one memory figure, one space figure, and the
// three things the engine asks of the hardware. Numbers only, no lab report.
---

<Section
  id="device-run"
  label="Device"
  title={"Two megabytes of flash history, 1,648 bytes of working memory."}
  lede="On an ESP32-S3, a chip with 8 MB of flash, a run wrote a record and read it back after four restarts. A boot does no storage work to find it: the address is computed from the fields, so there is no index to rebuild, and the memory it needs does not grow with the history."
>
  <figure class="device">
    <div class="device__frame">
      <img
        src="/esp32s3-board.jpg"
        alt="An ESP32-S3-WROOM-1 module on a flight-controller board, with its battery and USB bridge attached."
        width="1440"
        height="739"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </div>
    <figcaption>
      An ESP32-S3-WROOM-1 with 8 MB of flash, running from its own lithium cell.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="charts">
    <figure class="chart">
      <figcaption class="chart__title">Working memory, bytes</figcaption>
      <div class="chart__rows">
        <div class="chart__row">
          <span class="chart__key">First start</span>
          <span class="chart__val" data-count="2384">2,384</span>
          <span class="chart__track" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="chart__fill" style="--to: 1"></span>
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="chart__row">
          <span class="chart__key">Starts after</span>
          <span class="chart__val" data-count="1648">1,648</span>
          <span class="chart__track" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="chart__fill" style="--to: 0.691"></span>
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="chart__note">
        The first start prepares the storage. Later starts hold 1,648 bytes. What bounds it is one
        segment, and a segment's size is fixed.
      </p>
    </figure>

    <figure class="chart">
      <figcaption class="chart__title">Storage it occupies</figcaption>
      <div class="chart__rows">
        <div class="chart__row">
          <span class="chart__key">Region of the 8 MB flash</span>
          <span class="chart__val"><span data-count="2">2</span> MB</span>
          <span class="chart__track" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="chart__fill" style="--to: 0.25"></span>
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="chart__row">
          <span class="chart__key">Application in its 1 MiB slot</span>
          <span class="chart__val"><span data-count="447968">447,968</span> B</span>
          <span class="chart__track" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="chart__fill" style="--to: 0.4272"></span>
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="chart__note">
        A quarter of the flash and less than half its slot, with the bootloader untouched.
      </p>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <p class="close">
    It asks the hardware for three things: a region of flash, a write, and an erase. Everything above
    that is Ktema.
  </p>
  <p class="source">Measured on the board over four starts.</p>
</Section>

<script>
  import { resetAll, rollAll } from '../scripts/count-up';

  // The charts count up once, when the section is close enough to read, in the same
  // roll the decks use.
  const section = document.getElementById('device-run');

  if (section) {
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
      (entries) => {
        if (entries.some((entry) => entry.isIntersecting)) {
          resetAll(section);
          rollAll(section);
          observer.disconnect();
        }
      },
      { rootMargin: '0px 0px -30% 0px' },
    );
    observer.observe(section);
  }
</script>

<style>
  .device {
    max-width: 560px;
    margin: 40px 0 36px;
  }

  .device__frame {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 1440 / 739;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--bg-2);
  }

  .device img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .device figcaption {
    padding-top: 12px;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--fg-3);
  }

  .charts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 40px 48px;
  }

  .chart {
    margin: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-2);
    padding-top: 16px;
  }

  .chart__title {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--fg-3);
  }

  .chart__rows {
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-top: 16px;
  }

  .chart__row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    gap: 6px 16px;
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  .chart__key {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--fg-3);
  }

  .chart__val {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .chart__track {
    position: relative;
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    height: 12px;
    background: var(--bg-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .chart__fill {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 auto 0 0;
    width: calc(var(--to, 1) * 100%);
    background: var(--accent);
  }

  .chart__note {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--fg-3);
  }

  .close {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--fg-2);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .source {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--fg-3);
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .charts {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 28px;
    }
  }
</style>
